@startuml
title D-01 ExitPass v1.3 Logical Architecture
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 220

actor "Parker" as Parker
actor "Cashier" as Cashier
actor "Operator / Supervisor" as Operator
actor "Management / Auditor" as Management

rectangle "Channel Layer" {
  component "Centralized WebPay\ncustomer payment surface" as WebPay
  component "Assisted Payment Terminal\nCashier + Continuity modes" as APT
}

rectangle "Governance and Visibility" {
  component "Operator Console\nnon-payment governance" as Console
  component "Management Dashboard\nvisibility / reporting only" as Dashboard
}

rectangle "Trusted Core Platform" {
  component "Central PMS\npayment finality + ExitAuthorization authority" as Central
  component "Discount Workflow\npolicy resolution + payable basis update" as Discount
  component "Audit / Event Capability\noutbox-style durable facts" as Audit
  component "Reconciliation Workflow\npost-restoration + exception closure" as Recon
}

rectangle "Integration Boundaries" {
  component "Payment Orchestrator\nprovider outcome verification" as POA
  component "Vendor PMS Connector Instance\nprojection + live tariff integration" as Connector
  component "Gate / Exit Integration\nconsume authorization" as Gate
}

cloud "Payment Provider" as Provider
cloud "Vendor PMS / HCP\nraw session + normal tariff authority" as Vendor
component "Resolved Site POS Server\nSales Invoice fiscal authority" as POS

Parker --> WebPay : lookup / pay / view status
Cashier --> APT : assisted payment workflow
Operator --> Console : review / approve / govern
Management --> Dashboard : view / export / report

WebPay --> Central : scope-bound payment flow
APT --> Central : terminal workflow + status
Console --> Central : governance actions and review
Dashboard --> Central : labeled read models

Central --> Discount : statutory validation policy
Central --> POA : payment attempt coordination
POA --> Provider : provider interaction
POA --> Central : verified provider outcome

Central --> Connector : session / tariff / projection boundary
Connector --> Vendor : vendor-specific integration
Central --> POS : fiscal issuance request
POS --> Central : fiscal status / identity
Central --> Gate : ExitAuthorization
Gate --> Central : gate outcome

Central --> Audit : authoritative state changes
POA --> Audit : verified outcome facts
POS --> Audit : fiscal result facts
Connector --> Audit : health / freshness facts
Console --> Audit : governance facts
Dashboard --> Audit : access / export facts
Audit --> Recon : reconciliation evidence

note right of Central
Central PMS owns platform payment finality,
fiscal reference recording, degraded decisions
under approved policy, and ExitAuthorization.
end note

note bottom of POS
POS Server is fiscal authority only.
It does not declare finality or authorize exit.
end note

note bottom of Dashboard
Reporting consumes labeled sources.
It is not financial, fiscal, or exit authority.
end note
@enduml
